%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 24cee7e49fc532a45ab71bd5ace6cb7b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lines:
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: As you know, waking a well takes a special, limited resource
      called "Oasis Sand."
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC54C\uB2E4\uC2DC\uD53C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC744 \uB6AB\uAE30 \uC704\uD574\uC120
      '\uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798'\uB77C\uB294 \uD2B9\uC218\uD558\uACE0
      \uD55C\uC815\uB41C \uC790\uC6D0\uC744 \uC368\uC57C \uB3FC\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: But why do we need sand, of all things, to wake a well? I still
      don't get it.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uADFC\uB370, \uC65C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC744 \uB6AB\uB294 \uB370
      \uB610 \uBAA8\uB798\uB97C \uC368\uC57C \uB418\uC9C0? \uC544\uC9C1\uB3C4 \uC774\uD574\uAC00
      \uC548 \uB418\uB124."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: ...You've been doing this for three years, and you're asking
      that now?
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "...\uC774 \uC77C\uC744 3\uB144\uC774\uB098 \uD588\uB2E4\uBA74\uC11C
      \uAC11\uC790\uAE30 \uADF8\uB7F0 \uC18C\uB9AC\uB97C \uD558\uB294 \uAC70\uC608\uC694?"
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: It gives the parched ground a jolt so the water deep underground
      can find a way up...
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uBA54\uB9C8\uB978 \uB545\uC5D0 \uC790\uADF9\uC744 \uC918\uC11C
      \uAE4A\uC219\uD55C \uACF3\uC5D0 \uC788\uB294 \uBB3C\uAE38\uC744 \uC704\uB85C
      \uD2B8\uC774\uAC8C \uD558\uB294..."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: I mean... something like that? That's roughly how it works, right?
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uBB50... \uB300\uCDA9 \uADF8\uB7F0 \uC6D0\uB9AC\uC758 \uC18C\uC7AC
      \uC544\uB2C8\uC5C8\uC5B4\uC694?"
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: That's pretty vague. I still don't get it.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB108\uBB34 \uB300\uCDA9\uC778\uB370. \uC5EC\uC804\uD788 \uC774\uD574\uAC00
      \uC548 \uAC00."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Anyway, you can only drop Oasis Sand inside this area here.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC544\uBB34\uD2BC \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB294
      \uC5EC\uAE30 \uC774 \uBD80\uBD84, \uC774 \uC601\uC5ED \uC548\uC5D0\uB9CC \uB5A8\uC5B4\uD2B8\uB9B4
      \uC218 \uC788\uC5B4\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: There's a limit to how much you can use at once, so use it carefully,
      a little at a time!
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uD55C \uBC88\uC5D0 \uC4F8 \uC218 \uC788\uB294 \uC591\uC740
      \uC815\uD574\uC838 \uC788\uC73C\uB2C8, \uC870\uAE08\uC529 \uC2E0\uC911\uD558\uAC8C
      \uC0AC\uC6A9\uD574\uC57C \uB3FC\uC694!"
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: Right. Managing how much you use is the whole trick. You're much
      better at that than I am.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB9DE\uC544. \uC591 \uC870\uC808\uC744 \uC798\uD558\uB294 \uAC8C
      \uD575\uC2EC\uC774\uC57C. \uADF8\uAC74 \uB098\uBCF4\uB2E4 \uB108\uAC00 \uD6E8\uC52C
      \uB354 \uC798\uD558\uB294 \uAC83 \uAC19\uC544."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Once you've used a certain amount of Oasis Sand, mud starts building
      up in response.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC77C\uC815\uB7C9\uC758 \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB97C
      \uC0AC\uC6A9\uD558\uACE0 \uB098\uBA74, \uADF8\uC5D0 \uB300\uD55C \uBC18\uC751\uC73C\uB85C
      \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC5EC\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Tessa
    dialogueTextEN: Mud is a good sign. It means the ground's getting wet. But let
      too much build up in one spot, and it'll clog the well right back up.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD14C\uC0AC"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC9C4\uD759\uC740 \uB545\uC774 \uBB3C\uC5D0 \uC816\uACE0 \uC788\uB2E4\uB294
      \uC88B\uC740 \uC2E0\uD638\uC9C0\uB9CC, \uBC18\uB300\uB85C \uD55C \uACF3\uC5D0
      \uB108\uBB34 \uC313\uC774\uBA74 \uB3C4\uB85C \uC6B0\uBB3C\uC774 \uB9C9\uD600\uBC84\uB824."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Exactly! So we need to link the Oasis Sand together before the
      mud links up.
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uB9DE\uC544\uC694! \uADF8\uB7EC\uB2C8 \uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC5EC\uC11C
      \uC11C\uB85C\uB97C \uC787\uAE30 \uC804\uC5D0, \uC624\uC544\uC2DC\uC2A4 \uBAA8\uB798\uB85C
      \uC11C\uB85C\uB97C \uC774\uC5B4\uC57C \uD574\uC694."
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: Line up five or more squares horizontally, vertically, or diagonally,
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uAC00\uB85C, \uC138\uB85C, \uB300\uAC01\uC120 \uBC29\uD5A5\uC73C\uB85C
      5\uCE78 \uC774\uC0C1\uC744 \uC5F0\uC18D\uC73C\uB85C \uC774\uC73C\uBA74"
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
  - hasDialogue: 1
    speakerNameEN: Piper
    dialogueTextEN: and you'll give the ground enough of a jolt before the mud can
      build up!
    speakerNameKR: "\uD30C\uC774\uD37C"
    dialogueTextKR: "\uC9C4\uD759\uC774 \uC313\uC774\uAE30 \uC804\uC5D0 \uB545\uC5D0
      \uCDA9\uBD84\uD55C \uC790\uADF9\uC744 \uC904 \uC218 \uC788\uC744 \uAC70\uC608\uC694!"
    portrait: {fileID: 0}
    changeBackground: 0
    background: {fileID: 0}
    changePanel: 0
    characterPanel: {fileID: 0}
    changeBgm: 0
    bgm: {fileID: 0}
